@startuml

title The completion event

class "completion event" as completion <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    +step identifier : text
    +outcome : text
    +result : text
    +error : text
    +log entries : list
}

class "log entry" as log_entry <<value>> #F7E5FF {
    +item : text
    {field} +what happened : text
}

completion *-- log_entry : per-item log

note top of completion
Reports one step's outcome: the handler tells the engine how the step ended.
- step identifier: echoes the identifier on the command.
- outcome: success, success with warnings, or failure.
- result: what the step produced; empty on failure.
- error: why the step failed; empty on success.
- log entries: one entry per item the step could not do cleanly.
end note

note right of log_entry
One item of a step's work and what happened to it.
- item: the item the step acted on.
- what happened: the outcome for that item.
end note

@enduml
